 high degree  of autonomy  now Hong Kong has been returned to China  and are you telling me that the second  part is now void I mean that doesn't  make sense so I think this is important  not only for Hong Kong Hong Kong will  find its way forward and we want to  build our future on the promise of the  basic law and if this is not going on  then people have to ask how will they  how would they safeguard their future  but for the world there is a greater  significance  how can an international bilateral  treaty be unilaterally declared to be  void by one of the signing parties yeah  and what does it tell about the  reliability of China as it partners when  you think about the rule of law you know  then this is a country refuses to be  bound by the very treaty that it has  signed and now it says that it only the  returning Hong Kong to China part is  bilateral the other part is unilateral  then you have to think about China again  you have to look at China in a new light  what kind of an international player it  is but I think the more practical part  of it is this that is the people the  whole world cared about the joint  declaration 30 years ago because so many  international community members of  community was trading in Hong Kong they  were living in Hong Kong they were doing  business in Hong Kong the international  press was in Hong Kong if you want to  learn anything about China Hong Kong is  the best place now are you going to  change all that are you going to say  that none of this will be maintained and  if so how is the world going to do  business in Hong Kong with China or with  each other there are some people who  think that because China is now  economically successful Hong Kong is now  dispensable I do  think that this is the case at all and  if you ask people who do business in  Hong Kong it is because they rely on the  legal system they rely on the rule of  law they know that their rights are  protected by law they know that there is  freedom of information and if that is  why when the freedom of the press is  affected people sit up and say they get  really concerned so I don't think that  it is a matter of just for Hong Kong  people because they want democracy  because they want to have a control over  their own city which i think is all very  legitimate but also because what is Hong  Kong going to become if Hong Kong cannot  run its own systems  so all this looks a bit depressing but  from what I gather is that the students  are not depressed although the movement  has ended yeah I am not depressed I have  to say that although it is it is you're  right that it is depressing to see this  there's so much pressure and there's so  much the China is being so very stubborn  and so difficult to communicate refuses  to communicate that its priorities are  so very different from Hong Kong's  priorities and matters are urgent and we  find it very difficult to move forward  all these are very depressing but I'm  not depressed in for two reasons one is  that the world is noticing Hong Kong  again they start to us again is the  joint declaration spent do we now still  need the guarantee that China is going  to honor its promise an international  concern is extremely important secondly  the second date the new generation has  brought a new energy they are no longer  prepared to sit there and wait for  democracy to come to them they are no  longer content for someone else to look  after the rule of law they are prepared  to give their energy into the future of  Hong Kong to protect these systems and I  think this is wonderful you know if you  don't if you don't struggle for your  future you have no hope  democracy will never be given to you on  a plate  and the rule of law will not be  maintained  just at because they did the government  thinks that it is a good thing you've  got to protect it all the time eternal  vigilance and they've learned how  important it is they've gone through the  umbrella movement I don't think that  they are going to be the same people  again so we have a very energetic and  very very well I think they have very  mature minds and they have been sort of  transformed by this experience they have  been utterly transformed by the  experience and there is a new bonding  there and I don't think anybody can take  that away mm-hmm  well on that hopeful note thank you very  much my girl thank you for coming to a  studio thank you
 

